✅ LONGEST SUBSTRING WITH AT MOST K DISTINCT CHARACTERS

This is a step-up from classic sliding window and interviewers use it to see if you really understand window shrinking logic.

📌 Problem Statement

Given a string s and an integer k, find the length of the longest substring that contains at most k distinct characters.

🔹 Example 1
Input:  s = "eceba", k = 2
Output: 3
Explanation: "ece"

🔹 Example 2
Input:  s = "aa", k = 1
Output: 2

🧠 Core Idea (Interview Insight)

Use sliding window

Expand right

If distinct characters > k → shrink from left

Track maximum window length

🛠️ Algorithm (Step-by-Step)
Step 1: Two pointers
left = 0
right = 0

Step 2: HashMap to store char frequencies
Map<Character, Integer> freq

Step 3: Expand window

Add s[right] to map

If map size > k → shrink window

Step 4: Shrink window

Decrease frequency of s[left]

Remove from map if frequency becomes zero

Move left forward

⏱ Complexity

Time: O(n)

Space: O(k)

☕ Java Code (Clean & Interview-Ready)
class Solution {
    public int lengthOfLongestSubstringKDistinct(String s, int k) {
        if (k == 0 || s.length() == 0) return 0;

        Map<Character, Integer> freq = new HashMap<>();
        int left = 0, maxLen = 0;

        for (int right = 0; right < s.length(); right++) {
            char c = s.charAt(right);
            freq.put(c, freq.getOrDefault(c, 0) + 1);

            while (freq.size() > k) {
                char leftChar = s.charAt(left);
                freq.put(leftChar, freq.get(leftChar) - 1);

                if (freq.get(leftChar) == 0) {
                    freq.remove(leftChar);
                }
                left++;
            }

            maxLen = Math.max(maxLen, right - left + 1);
        }

        return maxLen;
    }
}

